\f0\fs26 \cf0 Build a site that displays as an animated menu that\'92s generated by values in a spreadsheet.\
\
The spreadsheet is called \'93menu.xlsx\'94\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 It should match the visual of "Menu Mockup.png\'94.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Column 1 dictates the title of the menu, which is displayed in the white area of the frame.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The next column dictates the scroll speed of galaxy-bg.jpg, which should scroll from left to right slowly. When the left edge is almost visible in the transparent space of frame.png, it should fade into a new copy of galaxy-bg.jpg that starts scrolling from left to right again.\
\
The next column dictates the speed of the transition between items, in seconds.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The next column dictates the hex code of the default menu item highlight.\
\
The next column dictates the hex cold of the \'93new\'94 menu item highlight.\
\
The next column dictates the names of the food items.\
\
The next column is the price.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The next column is the description.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The next column flags whether the item is new. If 1, item gets the \'93Highlight color (new)\'94 highlight, and \'93new\'94 sticker appears in the bottom right. If 0, it gets the \'93Highlight color (default)\'94 color.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The next column is the filename of the hero image that should accompany the item.\
\
The graphical elements are contained within the \'93assets\'94 folder.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The hero images are contained within the \'93food-pics\'94 folder.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 With those specifics in mind, here is the intended behavior of the menu:\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Matching the visual of \'93Menu Mockup.png\'94, the menu should cycle through highlighting each of the items in the list by highlighting them one by one and displaying the appropriate \'93food-pic\'94 image in the blank space on the right.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The \'93speed\'94 column will dictate how long each frame of the slideshow shows, in seconds.\
\
The site should display natively at 1920x1080. Do not worry about other breakpoints.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The site uses Roboto Bold as the main font.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 If there is no image in the image column, do not throw an error, just ignore it. \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Most importantly, the text should format intelligently based on the amount of text. All items and descriptions should fit vertically within the 1920 x 1080 breakpoint outlined earlier. If the user adds a new item, price and description to the bottom of the spreadsheet, text should format intelligently, scaling down the font sizes unilaterally.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 galaxy-bg should be the rear-most layer, then frame, then logo, then food-pics, then new-sticker (if an item is flagged as new.)}